From a53c3e1d7ac24762dbb86b7a380a0f8998f0fed9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:46:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/40] demux: adaptive: give a stream another chance when
 seeking

A stream whose demuxer fails to start is marked invalid so doBufferize()
does not retry every pass, and nothing ever marks it valid again.
setPosition() skips invalid streams and gives up when none are left, and
HLS usually has one stream per variant, so a single transient failure
leaves the session unseekable with the demux object still open.

A seek is a new attempt rather than a continuation of the loop the guard
protects, so clear it there. If starting still fails the stream is marked
invalid again at once, costing one attempt per seek rather than a spin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp b/modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp
index d476d77f2b..645063e336 100644
--- a/modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp
+++ b/modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp
@@ -152,6 +152,8 @@ bool AbstractStream::resetForNewPosition(vlc_tick_t seekMediaTime)
     inrestart = false;
     needrestart = false;
     discontinuity = false;
+    /* A seek is a fresh attempt; the failure paths raise this again. */
+    valid = true;
     if(!demuxer || demuxer->needsRestartOnSeek()) /* needs (re)start */
     {
         delete currentChunk;
